  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, yes, that is why I came today. The tablets, they gave me for five days. I took the first one on Tuesday... no, no, Thursday, sorry, it was Thursday, and by the evening I was having the hives all over my back.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:25",
      "end_timestamp": "00:50",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Wait, wait, let me think. It started with A. Amoxyclav, no... Amoxil... the doctor there said it was amoxicillin. Yes. Amoxicillin. I took a photo of the box, but my phone is in the car.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:24",
      "end_timestamp": "01:42",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Only one tablet. Amlodipine, 5 mg, once daily in the morning. Wait, is it 5 or 10? No, 5. I am sure it is 5, I keep the strip in my wallet.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:52",
      "end_timestamp": "03:07",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Blood pressure is 130 over 80, and the temperature is 37.0, so quite normal.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:46",
      "end_timestamp": "03:53",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Within the shared hospital records it usually travels, but the safest thing is that you also tell any doctor or pharmacist yourself. I'd suggest writing it in your phone and your wallet, next to the amlodipine strip.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:40",
      "end_timestamp": "05:02",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Excellent. There's also a more interesting question, which is whether you are truly allergic or whether the hives came from something else that week. I would like to arrange an allergy skin test, to find out for sure.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:15",
      "end_timestamp": "05:34",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "The usual simple painkillers are fine. The only ones to avoid for now are penicillin-type antibiotics, until the test says otherwise.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:14",
      "end_timestamp": "06:24",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    }
